  "body": "What happens (user report, v0.26.0 on macOS, 2026-11-23): in the Machines pane, the user clicked \"Tormach 770MX (ML)\" in the list. The row turned blue, but the Browser's Machine row stayed \"VMC 3-AXIS\". The user looked for an apply button and could not find one. The button \"Use for this setup\" exists. It is the first item of the details area under the list (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/machines_pane.rs`, `USE_FOR_SETUP`). When the details area is scrolled down (Max tool diameter, Coolants, Posts), the button is out of view. Nothing tells the user that a click only selects.\n\nExpected: the user can mount the selected machine without searching for the button.\n\nSuggested fix (smallest first):\n1. Draw \"Use for this setup\" outside the details scroll area, for example on the button row next to \"Edit machine\". It must stay visible at any scroll position, enabled or disabled with its \"Cannot assign: ...\" hover text as now.\n2. A double-click on a list row runs the same undoable assign (the same command as the button, so Ctrl+Z undoes it).\n3. When the selected machine differs from the setup's machine, show one line under the list: \"Selected: <name> - not yet this setup's machine\".\n\nWorkaround: scroll the details area to the top and click \"Use for this setup\".\n\nDone means: with the details scrolled to the bottom, \"Use for this setup\" is still visible and works. A double-click on a row mounts the machine, and undo restores the previous one. The UI structural tests (`crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/`) pin both.\n",
